</given-names></name><name><surname>Cunningham</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Gordon</surname><given-names>FC</given-names></name><name><surname>Field</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Clinical skills in junior medical officers: a comparison of self-reported confidence and observed competence</article-title><source>Med Educ</source><year>2004</year><volume>38</volume><fpage>358</fpage><lpage>367</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15025637</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1365-2923.2004.01773.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Coberly</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Goldenhar</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ready or not, here they come: acting interns' experience and perceived competency performing basic medical procedures</article-title><source>J Gen Intern Med</source><year>2007</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>491</fpage><lpage>494</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17372798</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s11606-007-0107-6</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>McArdle</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>O'Neill</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>How well prepared are graduates for the role of pre-registration house officer? A comparison of the perceptions of new graduates and educational supervisors</article-title><source>Med Educ</source><year>2001</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>578</fpage><lpage>584</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11380861</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1365-2923.2001.00955.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group perso